The canonical ("Conanical"?) barbarian, as written by Robert E Howard,
did in fact wear other armors.  In _Hour of the Dragon_, as king of
Aquilonia he wore full plate -- armor complete enough that when he'd
been struck down (by magic IIRC) one of his retainers went into battle
in his stead to keep his forces' morale up.

In other stories (I don't remember if these were canon, by REH, or
pastiches by other authors) he was described as wearing other forms of
armor, including scale mail and chainmail.

OTOH, I don't know how much of the Barbarian class is modeled on Conan
specifically... but genre suggests that heavier armors are still within
character.  Conan was usually limited more by availability of armor than
by personal preference.


